ASM17 - Self-Hosting 6502 Assembler
====================================

(Called ASM23 before the chain was renumbered to 00-17 on 2026-02-13.)

Architecture
------------

Two-pass assembler with hash tables for labels and instructions.

  Pass 1: Collect labels and macro definitions. Record forward references.
  Pass 2: Resolve all references and emit code.

The pass is tracked via PASS: $00 = pass 1, $FF = pass 2. Code tests bit 7
(BIT PASS / BMI) to distinguish passes.


Register Conventions
--------------------

  X - Output file handle. Preserved across most calls.
  Y - General-purpose index. Usually clobbered.
  A - Accumulator. Clobbered unless documented otherwise.


Memory Map
----------

  $0000-$00FF   Zero page variables (allocated via .zeropage sections)
  $0100-$01FF   6502 hardware stack
  $0200-$03FF   Forward reference list (512 bytes)
  $0400-$04FF   Free (was a separate label scope stack pre-Phase-3.6;
                macro activation state now lives on the source stack)
  $0500-$05FF   Free (was a 256-byte macro argument buffer pre-Phase-4.10)
  $0600-$067F   TOKEN buffer (128 bytes)
  $0680-$068F   ELSE_SEEN_ARRAY (16 bytes, one per .ifdef nesting level;
                accessed as ELSE_SEEN_ARRAY - 1,Y with Y = COND_DEPTH
                1..16, so all 16 bytes are used)
  $0690-$06AF   Free (was MACRO_ACTIVATION, a 32-byte staging buffer
                for the per-macro activation payload, until expand_macro
                switched to writing parsed slots directly into the new
                macro frame's payload region)
  $0700-$07FF   LHASHTAB - Label hash table (128 two-byte entries)
  $0800-$08FF   IFDEF_DECISIONS buffer (256 bytes)
  $2000+        Code section:
                  IHASHTAB (instruction hash table, from inst.asm.out)
                  Instruction/directive data (from inst.asm.out)
                  Assembler code
                  HEAP (immediately after code, grows upward via MEMP16)
  $F000         SOURCE_STACK (grows downward via SS_P16)
  $FFFC-$FFFF   Reset and interrupt vectors

The heap (MEMP16) grows upward storing hash entries, macro definitions, and
forward references. The source stack (SS_P16) grows downward storing
include/macro source contexts. A 256-byte safety buffer is maintained between
them for indexed addressing; err_out_of_memory is raised on collision.


Key Global State
----------------

  CURR_CHAR               Last character read by read_char
                           (alias for SS_CURR_CHAR)
  TOKEN            $0600  Buffer holding current token being parsed
  PASS                    $00 = pass 1, $FF = pass 2
  PC16                    Current program counter
  MEMP16                  Heap pointer (grows upward)
  SS_P16                  Source stack pointer (grows downward)
  HEX16 / OPERAND16      Current parsed value (aliased names)
  IS_FWDREF               $FF if current value is a forward reference
  INST_PTR16 /            Instruction table entry or macro definition
    MACRO_DEF_PTR16        pointer (aliased)
  IN_MACRO_DEF            $FF while capturing macro body
  LABEL_SCOPE16           Current scope identifier for local labels

All are zero page except TOKEN.


Parsing Model
-------------

  - read_char advances input and stores the result in both A and CURR_CHAR.
  - Token reading fills the TOKEN buffer with a null terminator.
  - Single-character lookahead via CURR_CHAR drives parsing decisions.
  - check_for_end_of_line skips spaces and checks for end-of-line or comment.


Hash Tables
-----------

Two hash tables are used, both with 128 two-byte entries (256 bytes each):

IHASHTAB (Instruction hash table) -- Pre-generated by instgen.asm and
included as out/inst.asm.out. Contains mnemonics, addressing mode/opcode
data, and directive handler addresses. Read-only at runtime; no initialization
needed.

LHASHTAB (Label hash table) -- Built at runtime during assembly. Stores
global labels, local labels (under a global scope), and macro definitions.
Macro **parameters** are NOT in LHASHTAB -- they live in activation slots
on the macro's source-stack frame (see Macro System / Source Stack below).
Entries are allocated on the heap.

Hash entries on the heap have the format:

  [next_ptr_lo] [next_ptr_hi] [key...] $00 [value_lo] [value_hi]

Local and macro-local labels use an escape format with type byte and scope:

  [next_ptr_lo] [next_ptr_hi] [type] [scope_lo] [scope_hi] [name...] $00
    [value_lo] [value_hi]

  type = LABEL_TYPE_LOCAL ($01)        -- local label under enclosing
                                          global label scope
       = LABEL_TYPE_MACRO_LOCAL ($03)  -- macro-local label scoped by
                                          EXPANSION_ID

common.asm provides select_label_hash_table and
select_instruction_hash_table to switch between the two tables.


Instruction Table Generation
-----------------------------

instgen.asm is a separate program (assembled by the previous version's
assembler) that reads instruction and directive definitions from
instruction_tables.asm, builds a hash table in memory, and outputs assembly
source code (out/inst.asm.out) that recreates the table as static data.

The assembler includes this generated file first (at $2000) so the tables
sit on a page boundary. This avoids runtime initialization and keeps the
assembler smaller.


Forward References
------------------

When pass 1 encounters a label reference before the label is defined, it
records the current PC in the forward reference list (FWDREF_LIST,
$0200-$03FF). The list is an array of 16-bit PC values terminated by $FFFF.

In pass 2, check_forward_ref compares the current PC against the next entry
in the list. When they match, the assembler forces absolute addressing mode
even if the resolved value would fit in zero page. This ensures pass 2 emits
the same instruction sizes as pass 1.

An assignment (label = value) is stored in pass 1, so it can only use labels
defined before it: pass 1 takes a label not defined yet as 0. Pass 2
evaluates the value again, with every label defined, and stops with error
43, "Assignment uses a label defined later", if it differs from the stored
one, rather than let the wrong value through.

"* =" and ".reserve" move the PC in pass 1 too, so one that uses a label
defined later moves everything after it differently in the two passes.
Pass 2 compares each label's address (global, local and macro-local) with
the one pass 1 stored, and stops with error 44, "Address differs between
passes", at the first that differs. A shift with no label after it is not
reported, and does no harm: nothing refers to the addresses it moved.


Macro System
------------

Definition (macro_capture.asm): The .macro directive stores parameter names
and the macro body on the heap. The value region of a macro hash entry
starts with a single-byte parameter count, then the param names
(null-separated), then the body:

  [N] [param1\0] [param2\0] ... [paramN\0] [body\0]

Expand-time consumers read N from the count byte and walk N names; no
trailing empty-string sentinel is needed. dir_macro enforces
MACRO_MAX_ARGS = 32 at definition time so the count byte can't overflow.
During capture, the body is compressed (comments stripped, consecutive
spaces collapsed, string/char literals preserved verbatim). Nested .macro
directives are rejected. In pass 2, the body is skipped since it was
already captured in pass 1.

Expansion (macro_expansion.asm): Macro invocation reads N from the def,
pre-checks that the new frame fits (worst-case frame_size = 19 + name_len
+ 3*N <= 255; 8-byte fixed header + 11-byte scope tail), then writes
parsed slot values directly into the
unallocated source-stack memory just below SS_P16 -- the area that will
become the new frame's payload once the push commits. SS_P16 / SS_SRC_TYPE
/ SS_MEM_PTR16 / SS_CURR_LINE16 stay unchanged during arg parsing, so the
parent's source remains active for read_char and any error fires with the
correct line and frame name.

The frame is reserved up front via ss_reserve_frame, which performs the
OOM check and writes frame_size, the fixed header (curr_type, prev_type,
prev_line), and the macro name into the pending region -- all before
argument parsing, so TOKEN is then free to be clobbered. After all args
are written and the 11-byte scope tail (LABEL_SCOPE16, CACHED_HASH,
prev_macro_lookup, the previous lookup slot/param pointers, and
MACRO_ENTRY16) is appended, ss_commit_pending_frame commits the frame:
it captures the parent's current read state into prev_data, advances
SS_P16 := SS_PEND_P16, and sets SS_SRC_TYPE = MEMORY. The new scope
(EXPANSION_ID16, LABEL_SCOPE16, CACHED_HASH, SCOPE_DEPTH) is set up only
after the parent's scope_block has been captured into the frame, and the
lookup pointer triple (MACRO_LOOKUP_FRAME16 / _SLOTS16 / _PARAMS16) is
anchored at the new frame last so the body's identifier lookups find
this frame in O(1).

Identifier resolution (expressions.asm: resolve_identifier): when SCOPE_DEPTH
> 0, lookup reads MACRO_LOOKUP_FRAME16 (the innermost macro frame's
address), points TABP16 at it, and calls ss_lookup_param_slot. That
function pulls MACRO_ENTRY16 from the frame's tail, reads N from the
def's count byte, scans the N param names for a match, and -- on a hit --
reads the slot at the corresponding position in the frame's payload.
Misses fall through to LHASHTAB. The pointer-based frame lookup is O(1)
per identifier, regardless of how many .include or macro frames are
stacked on top, since file pushes don't touch MACRO_LOOKUP_FRAME16.

Scoping: Each expansion gets a unique LABEL_SCOPE16 from the monotonic
EXPANSION_ID16 counter. Local labels (.name) within a macro are scoped to
that expansion. Parameters shadow global labels of the same name. Outer-
macro parameters are NOT visible to an inner macro -- lookup uses only
MACRO_LOOKUP_FRAME16 (single innermost frame).

Recursion detection: check_macro_recursion walks the prev_macro_lookup
chain threaded through each macro frame's payload, comparing each
frame's saved MACRO_ENTRY16 against the active one. File frames don't
appear in the chain so the walk skips them for free. Direct and indirect
recursion are both caught. Out-of-stack on deep nesting is reported as
err_out_of_memory rather than a separate macro-nesting limit.


Source Stack
----------

The source stack (source_stack.asm) handles two source types transparently:

  File sources (type 0): Read from a file handle via the emulator's I/O.
    Used for the main input and .include files.

  Memory sources (type 1): Read from a null-terminated buffer on the heap.
    Used for macro expansion.

Each frame begins with a 1-byte frame_size at offset 0; push allocates and
sets it, pop reads it and advances SS_P16, and chain walks step by adding
frame_size each iteration. Layout (low to high address within the frame):

  [0]      frame_size           total bytes in this frame
  [1]      curr_type            0 = file, 1 = memory
  [2]      prev_type            type we return to on pop
  [3..4]   prev_line_L/H        line number in parent
  [5..]    name\0               null-terminated source name
  ...      prev_data            1 byte (file handle) or 2 bytes
                                (parent's SS_MEM_PTR16)
  ...      payload              optional, memory frames only

Putting the type/line header at fixed offsets 1..4 (rather than after the
variable-length name) keeps the pop_source dispatch and ss_walk_frames
O(1) per frame for the type read.

For macro expansions, the payload trailing prev_data carries the macro
activation state. Slots and the scope tail are written directly into the
frame's reserved payload region by expand_macro -- there is no separate
staging buffer:

  parameter slots [0..N-1]   3 bytes each: fwdref, value_L, value_H
  scope tail (11 bytes):
    LABEL_SCOPE16 lo/hi      restored on pop
    CACHED_HASH              restored on pop
    prev_macro_lookup lo/hi  threads the macro-frame chain so
                             check_macro_recursion and
                             pop_label_scope_from_frame can walk
                             innermost-first in O(1) per step
    prev_macro_lookup_slots lo/hi
                             restored on pop; cached slot[0] pointer
                             kept in lockstep with MACRO_LOOKUP_FRAME16
    prev_macro_lookup_params lo/hi
                             restored on pop; cached param-name-list
                             pointer kept in lockstep with
                             MACRO_LOOKUP_FRAME16
    MACRO_ENTRY16 lo/hi      this expansion's macro definition; sits
                             at frame_size - 2..-1 so recursion check
                             reads it without further offset math

N is read from the macro definition (the count byte at MACRO_ENTRY16),
not from the frame -- there is no per-frame arg_count byte. The
source-stack entry point supporting this is:

  push_memory_source_reserve_payload reserves the payload region without
                                     copying (caller pre-wrote the bytes
                                     just below SS_P16 before the push)

Memory pop is dispatched through MEMORY_POP_HANDLER, a compile-time
equate the host program defines before including source_stack.asm. The
assembler points it at pop_label_scope_from_frame, which reads the scope
tail and restores LABEL_SCOPE16, CACHED_HASH, and the lookup pointer
triple (MACRO_LOOKUP_FRAME16 / _SLOTS16 / _PARAMS16) when the macro
frame is popped.


Conditional Assembly
--------------------

.ifdef, .ifndef, .else, and .endif control conditional assembly. Nesting up
to 16 levels is supported. When a condition is false, the assembler enters
skipping mode (SKIP_DEPTH > 0) where only conditional directives are
processed and all other content is ignored.

IFDEF_DECISIONS records pass 1 decisions so pass 2 can replay them
identically, even for labels that are now defined due to pass 1 collection.


Code Organization
-----------------

asm.asm is the top-level file. It defines memory layout constants, zero page
variables, includes all modules, and contains the assembly loop and entry
point.


Modules (included from asm.asm, in include order):

  out/inst.asm.out    Pre-generated instruction/directive hash table
  environment.asm     Emulator I/O entry points: file ops, console, args
  macros.asm          16-bit utility macros (INC16, CP16, CMP16, PUSH16, ...)
  common.asm          Mode constants, label types, heap; includes hash_table.asm
  label_scope.asm     Expansion ID counter, current scope state, and the
                      pop_label_scope_from_frame hook installed on the
                      source stack's memory-pop vtable
  forward_ref.asm     Forward reference list operations
  source_stack.asm      Unified file/memory source stack, read_char
  errors.asm          Error messages and handlers
  from_decimal.asm    Decimal string to 16-bit value conversion
  output.asm          PC management, byte emission
  tokenizer.asm       Character classification, token/hex reading, escapes
  expressions.asm     Expression evaluation, char literals, byte selectors
  labels.asm          Label capture, local labels, value assignment
  instructions.asm    Instruction lookup, operand parsing, emission
  directives.asm      Directive dispatch, data directives, conditionals
  macro_capture.asm   .macro directive processing, body capture
  macro_expansion.asm Macro invocation, argument parsing, scope setup
  init.asm            CLI argument processing, input file opening

Foundational modules (environment, macros, common, source stack, errors) come
first, followed by parsing and assembly modules, with init last.


Assembly Loop
-------------

The main loop in assemble_code processes input line by line:

  1. Read first character of line. EOF ends the pass.
  2. If capturing a macro body (IN_MACRO_DEF): delegate to capture_macro_line.
  3. If in skipping mode (SKIP_DEPTH > 0): only process conditional directives.
  4. Otherwise: capture label if line starts in column 0, then process
     directive or instruction/macro.


Configuration Aliases
---------------------

Several symbols are configured before their include file to customize
behavior:

  SS_NAME        = TOKEN              Source stack uses TOKEN for filenames
  read_char          = source_stack_read_char
  CURR_CHAR          = SS_CURR_CHAR
  HT_KEY             = TOKEN              Hash table key source
  HT_V16             = HEX16              Hash table value source


Debug Build
-----------

Assembling with define:enable_debug includes additional code:

  - Heap usage and forward reference count reporting
  - show_macros support for displaying captured macro definitions
  - small_heap argument for memory limit testing
  - Forward reference tracking verification between passes
